OL,3,CWhat is a dust devil and are we seeing
OL,4,Cmore of them in the UK?
OL,6,FHow is a dust devil different from a
OL,7,Ftornado?
OL,9,FAlthough they can appear similar, dust
OL,10,Fdevils and tornadoes form in very
OL,11,Fdifferent ways.
OL,13,FDust devils are generally much weaker
OL,14,Fthan tornadoes and develop on warm,
OL,15,Fsunny days beneath clear skies rather
OL,16,Fthan in thunderstorms.
OL,18,FThey rarely cause more than minor
OL,19,Fdisruption, although the strongest
OL,20,Fexamples can briefly lift lightweight
OL,21,Fobjects or reduce visibility.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/6
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
