OL,3,CWhat is a dust devil and are we seeing
OL,4,Cmore of them in the UK?
OL,6,FIt is most likely that a dust devil
OL,7,Fwill develop over surfaces that heat
OL,8,Fup quickly, such as dry fields,
OL,9,Fharvested farmland, beaches or large
OL,10,Fareas of tarmac.
OL,12,FMost go unnoticed because they're
OL,13,Fshort-lived and often form away from
OL,14,Fbuilt-up areas, but when one is
OL,15,Fspotted, it can be an impressive
OL,16,Freminder of how localised weather can
OL,17,Fbe.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/6
